window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["30"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/antigua-and-barbuda":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"2b18bd23d846758d23282b9f0e0531a68fad87aa11aaa7869c66034db6d2f11d","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/antigua-and-barbuda","bytes":61815,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Antigua and Barbuda travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-11T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-13T09:27:23+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/antigua-and-barbuda/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Antigua and Barbuda’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Antigua and Barbuda set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Antigua and Barbuda High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Antigua and Barbuda, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Antigua and Barbuda without a visa. On entry, you’ll be allowed to stay for a maximum period of 90 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["Visitors must be able to show an onward or return ticket in order to enter the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer (to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons), you must apply and pay for an extension of stay through the ",["Antigua and Barbuda Immigration Department","https://immigration.gov.ag/visa-services/general-visa-information/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to overstay the entry period or to work without a work permit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Antiguan and Barbudan authorities advise travellers to use ",["ArriveAntigua.com","https://arriveantigua.com/no_desktop"]," to speed up your entry into the country, though it is not mandatory. You can only access it through a mobile telephone or tablet and within 72 hours of travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most airlines include departure tax in their flight costs. If you’re flying on regional airlines, you should check whether tax is included before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Antigua and Barbuda, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Antigua and Barbuda guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/10/antigua-and-barbuda#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Antigua and Barbuda","https://vcbia.com/customs-and-immigration/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Antigua and Barbuda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Antigua and Barbuda, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of violent crime including murder, armed robbery and sexual assault in Antigua and Barbuda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to protect your personal safety. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure your accommodation is secure – this also applies if you are staying on a yacht"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when walking alone off the busy main roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid isolated areas, including beaches, particularly after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["only use licensed taxis"]},{"k":"li","s":["take particular care around large gatherings, including street and beach parties, especially after dark or during the festival season"]},{"k":"li","s":["not carry large amounts of cash or jewellery"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave valuables and travel documents in a safety deposit box or secure hotel safe"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that resisting a robbery can lead to a violent response, including use of weapons that can result in physical injury"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess drugs. There are severe penalties for all drug offences. Pack all luggage yourself and do not carry anything through customs for anyone else."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke in public places. You may face arrest for doing so."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Laws on clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for anyone, including children, to dress in camouflage clothing."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attitudes towards the LGBT+ community are mostly conservative in the Caribbean."]},{"k":"p","s":["Antigua and Barbuda no longer has legislation against same-sex sexual acts. However, showing affection in public may attract unwanted and negative attention. It is uncommon for opposite or same-sex couples to show affection in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming. Currents can be deceptively strong and not all beaches have lifeguards or warning flags. Monitor all beaches carefully and follow warnings. See ",["Royal National Lifeboat Institution safety advice","https://rnli.org/safety/respect-the-water"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Antigua and Barbuda, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need a temporary local driving licence to drive in Antigua and Barbuda. Your car hire company will usually help with this process or these can be obtained at the Transport Board or local police stations. You need to present a UK driving licence to get a local temporary licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads can have potholes and unmarked speed bumps. Minor roads and those in rural areas are narrow and can have blind corners. Pedestrians often walk on the roads. Drivers do not always use indicators."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care when driving at night, as some roads are unlit. Road signs and hazards may not be easily visible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not stop if pedestrians flag you down. Keep car doors locked when driving."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident, call the police and do not move the vehicle."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis are not metered. Standard taxi fares are set by zones. Agree the fare in local currency with the driver before you set off. You can often pay in US dollars as well as Eastern Caribbean dollars."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Visitors arriving by sea must contact the Antigua Port Authority at least 6 hours before arrival using VHF Channel 16. Follow instructions on which port or holding area to use to complete entry formalities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Passengers arriving by cruise liner are subject to the protocols placed on board by their cruise company."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season in the Caribbean normally runs from June to November. Monitor local and international weather updates from the Antigua and Barbuda Meteorological Services, the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/"]," and the US National Hurricane Center and follow the advice of the local authorities, including any evacuation orders."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["tropical cyclones","https://www.gov.uk/tropical-cyclones"]," for advice about how to prepare effectively and what to do if you are likely to be affected by a hurricane."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Antigua and Barbuda. Tremors are felt occasionally in the Caribbean. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 or 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company promptly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest information on ",["vaccine recommendations for Antigua and Barbuda","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/10/antigua-and-barbuda#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Antigua and Barbuda","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/10/antigua-and-barbuda"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Antigua and Barbuda"]},{"k":"p","s":["The main government hospital can cope with many types of treatment but serious cases may need an emergency evacuation. Medical treatment in Antigua and Barbuda can be expensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before choosing to be treated at a private facility, check their policies on pre-payment. Private clinics may not accept medical travel insurance as payment for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Antigua and Barbuda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/antigua-list-of-medical-facilities-practitioners"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Antigua and Barbuda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 or 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Antigua%20and%20Barbuda"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Antigua%20and%20Barbuda"]," in Antigua and Barbuda"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Antigua and Barbuda","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-antigua-and-barbuda"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Antigua and Barbuda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/antigua-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/antigua-and-barbuda/british-high-commission-st-johns"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/antigua-and-barbuda/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":11401,"change":"New information that it is illegal to smoke in public places ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahamas":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"a6093f09f9216835977be27ae84395e865abdd9c6bef4b99feeac96d7e2a1329","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bahamas","bytes":59185,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bahamas travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-04T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-28T17:01:45+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahamas/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of The Bahamas’ current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in The Bahamas set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact ",["The Bahamas High Commission in the UK","https://www.bahamashclondon.net/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter The Bahamas, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you plan to leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can usually stay in The Bahamas for up to 30 days without a visa. You can get ",["extensions up to a maximum of 8 months","https://www.immigration.gov.bs/entry-requirements/extension-of-stay/"],". Penalties for overstaying include a fine, detention and deportation. The Bahamas High Commission lists ",["more information about visas","https://www.bahamashclondon.net/forms/visa-applications/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive in The Bahamas from the USA, and you have an ",["Electronic System for Travel Authorization (ESTA)","https://esta.cbp.dhs.gov/esta"],", the time you spend in The Bahamas counts towards the 90 days you have on your ESTA. If you are in any doubt about your US visa status, ask the US Immigration and Naturalization Service or any US diplomatic mission before starting your return journey."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter The Bahamas, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bahamas guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/19/bahamas#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Bahamian Government issued a ",["Travel Advisory note","https://mofa.gov.bs/ebola-bundibugyo-virus-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-surrounding-countries/"]," which introduces health screening, possible quarantine or isolation measures for travellers who have visited affected regions within 30 days of their arrival to The Bahamas."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of The Bahamas","https://www.bahamascustoms.gov.bs/visitor-info/arriving/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in The Bahamas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in The Bahamas, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreigners. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been violent crimes and armed robberies, sometimes fatal, in residential and tourist areas of New Providence and Grand Bahama."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk, do not go on foot outside the main tourist areas and beaches, especially if you are alone. Stay in downtown Nassau, where there are regular police patrols. Avoid unlit areas, and travel in groups after dusk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care if travelling on local bus services at night away from the main tourist areas. If you are attacked, do not resist and comply with any demands. Robbers may have concealed weapons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increase in reported break-ins and thefts. The outlying islands of The Bahamas (known as the Family or Out Islands) have lower crime rates."]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of petty theft and pickpocketing increases during regattas and festivals. You can take precautions by keeping valuables in a safe place. Take care to lock doors and windows when staying at short-term vacation rental properties, especially if there are no security guards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of sexual assault increases during regattas and festivals. Do not leave your drinks unattended."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of sexual assaults on foreign nationals by jet ski operators in Nassau."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for possessing or trafficking drugs are severe. Tourists may encounter drugs in pubs and bars. Police are vigilant and you could face a substantial fine, deportation or imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local attitudes towards the LGBT+ community are mostly conservative throughout the Caribbean. In The Bahamas, same-sex sexual relations have been legal since 1991, with an age of consent of 18. However, LGBT+ travellers should be aware that showing affection in public may receive unwanted and negative attention. Showing affection in public, especially for same-sex couples, is uncommon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fatal shark attacks can happen without warning. Night swimming (including at dusk), puts you at a higher risk, even in shallow waters close to resorts. Paddle boards in deeper water could be at risk. The Bahamian authorities warn of a particular threat in New Providence and nearby islands and cays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some organisers of day excursions use bait to attract marine life, which can also increase the risk of sharks attacking. Never go into water that has been baited. Several attacks in wider Bahamian waters have been linked to tour operators offering shark encounters too close to where fishermen have been gutting fish."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of jet skis when swimming. Most swimming areas are marked by buoys, but these are not always respected by jet ski operators or tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["The water sports industry in The Bahamas is poorly regulated. Be careful when renting jet skis and other water sports equipment, as many companies and individuals offering water sports activities are unregistered or use poor quality equipment. People have been killed and seriously injured, or killed others, when using jet skis and other watercraft recklessly."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in The Bahamas for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying longer or living in The Bahamas, you’ll need to get a Bahamian driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although traffic drives on the left-hand side of the road, most vehicles, including hire cars, are imported from the USA and are left-hand drive."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal alcohol limit when driving is the same as in England, but this law is not always enforced – so driving in the evening and on rural roads may be dangerous."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season in The Bahamas normally runs from 1 June to 30 November. Hurricanes and resulting floods in The Bahamas can be deadly. In preparation for a hurricane, make sure your residence is secure, you have sufficient drinking water and access to life jackets in case there is a tidal surge."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Government of The Bahamas issues wireless emergency alerts directly to mobile phones and provides updates on the ",["Bahamas Department of Meteorology website","https://met.gov.bs/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Official shelters can be found ",["here","https://getready.gov.bs/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/2025-Hurricane-Shelter-List-DIR-20052025.pdf"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of flight cancellation, local residents tend to make departure plans well in advance of a possible evacuation order."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local weather updates and monitor approaching storms on the ",["US National Hurricane Center website","https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["how to respond to hurricane warnings","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 or 919 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for The Bahamas","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/19/bahamas#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in The Bahamas","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/19/bahamas"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"hs","s":["HIV and AIDS"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s estimated that at least 7,600 adults aged 15 or over in The Bahamas are living with HIV – around 3.2% of the adult population. This compares to around 0.3% in the UK. Take normal precautions to avoid exposure to HIV."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in The Bahamas"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in The Bahamas","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-in-bahamas"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical treatment is of a good standard but can be expensive. Emergency medical facilities are limited on all the Family Islands. Serious cases are transferred to Nassau or Freeport – or Miami, USA – by air ambulance. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/mental-health-and-wellbeing-abroad"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in The Bahamas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 or 919 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Bahamas"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=bahamas"]," in The Bahamas"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in The Bahamas","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-the-bahamas"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in The Bahamas","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bahamas-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bahamas/british-high-commission-nassau"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bahamas/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12120,"change":"New information about Ebola screening when arriving in country ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/the-government-has-delayed-the-toughest-spending-decisions-but-heres-what-we-do-know-after-the-budget-295491":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"03bebc7106f232ab770f56714edbb91dd5250e76f621eea547625989f4974244","read":"https://theconversation.com/the-government-has-delayed-the-toughest-spending-decisions-but-heres-what-we-do-know-after-the-budget-295491","bytes":182202,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"The government has delayed the toughest spending decisions – but here’s what we do know after the budget","by":[{"n":"Steve Schifferes","r":"Honorary Research Fellow, City Political Economy Research Centre, City St George's, University of London"}],"pub":"2026-10-30T16:17:05Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["John Healey’s steady-as-she-goes budget was a picture of a government doing its best to offer “what help we can afford”, while weathering the economic storms. But despite its 98 policy measures, decisions on some of the biggest issues appear to have been kicked down the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the meantime, it seems that the real incomes of UK households could fall by 1% next year. This forecast, from the ",["Office for Budget Responsibility","https://theconversation.com/topics/obr-130030"]," (OBR), offered a grim picture. It also predicted UK economic growth of ",["just 1%","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9x28350ly07o"],", as well as higher inflation and interest rates. The OBR, the government’s independent spending watchdog, has also suggested that ",["by 2029-30","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae1f7b839d29f3f9b9b3f36/economic-and-fiscal-outlook-october-2026-web-accessible.pdf#page=12"]," households will still be only 1% better off than they were ten years previously. This would be the slowest growth in real disposable household income for generations."]},{"k":"p","s":["And in further bad news for households, the OBR estimated that the tax collected by the government as a percentage of GDP would reach record levels by 2030-31 – ",["six percentage points higher","https://www.thisismoney.co.uk/money/article-16247497/Struggling-workers-pay-extra-income-tax-stealth-raids.html"]," than pre-pandemic levels. Taxes are already higher than at any time since the second world war."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget was ",["enthusiastically backed","https://labourlist.org/2026/10/budget-labour-members-poll-survation/"]," by Labour members. But it can also be seen as a holding operation by the chancellor, reassuring the markets while leaving the prime minister the space to develop his vision of the causes close to his heart. These of course include social care, devolution and welfare reform. Notably, the only measure which in relative terms was generously funded was the ",["£500 million","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae20b9039d29f3f9b9b3f55/E03668986_HMT_Budget_2026_TEXT_PRINT__1_.pdf#page=102"]," allocated to end rough sleeping, the cause Burnham cited as his priority on his first day in office."]},{"k":"p","s":["The limited measures to help with the cost of living reflect Burnham’s concerns about tackling the issue that ",["most worries the public","https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/wellbeing/bulletins/publicopinionsandsocialtrendsgreatbritain/august2026"],", but they are modest in scale and for the most part temporary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Budget 2026: experts on what John Healey’s ‘breathing space’ plan means for households","https://theconversation.com/budget-2026-experts-on-what-john-healeys-breathing-space-plan-means-for-households-295377"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The Treasury’s modest ambitions are reflected in the limited scale of the additional taxes it has announced to fund cost-of-living measures, especially to help with energy prices. The government has found some taxes it can raise and some efficiency savings it could make."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, most of the cost-of-living measures – which ",["will cost £6.5 billion","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae20b9039d29f3f9b9b3f55/E03668986_HMT_Budget_2026_TEXT_PRINT__1_.pdf#page=112"]," this year – are only temporary, while some of the tax increases occur later in the parliament. As a result, the government expects that within five years the situation will be reversed, with Treasury revenues ",["up by £7 billion","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae20b9039d29f3f9b9b3f55/E03668986_HMT_Budget_2026_TEXT_PRINT__1_.pdf#page=112"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["One move that could have a long-term impact is Healey’s changes to the spending rules to protect “preventive spending” from department cuts. These are measures that have an initial cost but eventually save money. An example is the ",["SureStart childcare programme","https://ifs.org.uk/publications/effect-sure-start-youth-misbehaviour-crime-and-contacts-childrens-social-care"],", for example, which has been shown to improve long-term education prospects and reduce crime in deprived communities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Back to welfare and defence"]},{"k":"p","s":["But the government has postponed its most difficult decisions – on defence, social care, devolution and welfare spending. The latter, the most politically challenging, awaits the publication of two key reports on welfare next month. The Timms and Milburn reviews will report respectively on personal independence payments, and the number of young people not in education, employment or training (Neet)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any big decisions are likely to take shape after the publication of the prime minister’s ten-year plan (expected in December), and next year’s spending review, which will flesh out spending plans up to the next general election."]},{"k":"p","s":["The urgent need to boost defence spending to 3% of GDP by 2030 was the issue that led ",["Healey to resign","https://theconversation.com/what-john-healeys-resignation-as-defence-secretary-means-for-keir-starmer-and-the-uk-285111"]," from the previous government. In his first budget as chancellor, despite insisting this target would be met, he was cagey on how it might be financed."]},{"k":"p","s":["He cited “innovative financing measures”, which might include off-the-books contributions from the private sector through PFI (private finance initiatives) and the use of government investment banks, which may not be subject to the same fiscal rules. Healey also sees defence spending as part of the government’s industrial strategy, and ministers have announced that foreign firms that win defence contracts of ",["more than £50 million","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/defence-contracts-to-prioritise-british-jobs-and-skills"]," will have to deliver benefits of the same amount back into the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another thing we do know is that defence investment will also be funded by forcing all other departments to cut their own spending ",["by 1%","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ynl0px107o"],". This is a pattern Healey may repeat to fund other new spending commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, the OBR estimates that, after taking into account the future spending plans of the “protected” departments (health, education and defence), all other departments would need to cut their own spending ",["by 2.6%","https://www.civilserviceworld.com/professions/article/budget-2026-unprotected-departments-face-26-realterms-cuts"]," to allow the government to meet its 2030-31 fiscal target. This would mean less for roads, prisons, the police, housing, and higher education. “Efficiency savings” would be unlikely to close the gap."]},{"k":"p","s":["The chancellor has taken over at a particularly difficult time for the world economy, and European nations are among the hardest hit. Healey will need luck as well as skill to navigate the shoals of a global slowdown. However, it is already clear that the prime minister’s desire for closer ties with Europe to boost growth ",["is not shared","https://www.ft.com/content/24a59c81-1e3d-4ff1-8856-2812f27985c3?syn-25a6b1a6=1"]," by the chancellor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many events – from a resumption of full-scale warfare in the Strait of Hormuz to the possible collapse of the AI bubble – are beyond Healey’s control. He has temporarily reassured the bond markets with his cautious “do no harm” budget. But delivering improved living standards and better public services to a still-jaundiced electorate remains an enduring challenge."]}],"chars":5608},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-26T18:34Z","sha":"c3ef49a4447edff40ba5b4a9b7adcef8c59418194e66b3a5527b52365a18e11b","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo","bytes":59524,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kosovo travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-13T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-23T12:48:46+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Large gatherings in Pristina and other urban centres"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large gatherings are taking place, including in Pristina in the evenings. This could lead to some disruption, including to traffic and public transport. Keep up to date with local developments, allow extra time for travel, and stay away from any large crowds or demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Kosovo set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Kosovan Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kosovo, your passport must be undamaged and valid for the duration of your stay. You do not need an additional period of validity beyond this."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kosovo-Serbia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Serbia do not consider the designated crossing points with Kosovo to be official international border crossing points."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, it is possible to travel from Serbia to Kosovo, and back again."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot travel from Kosovo to Serbia without a Serbian entry stamp from Belgrade, Niš or Kraljevo airports, or one of Serbia’s other border crossings with:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bosnia and Herzegovina"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bulgaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Croatia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Hungary"]},{"k":"li","s":["Montenegro"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Macedonia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are likely to be refused entry without a valid Serbian entry stamp. You should take a route through a third country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border guards have denied foreign nationals entry to Serbia if they have Republic of Kosovo stamps in their passports. We are also aware of isolated incidents where Serbian authorities have cancelled Kosovo stamps in passports of foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tensions between Serbia and Kosovo can cause difficulties at border crossings with Kosovo."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Kosovo without a visa for up to 90 days, for business or tourism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Officials may ask you to provide documentary evidence giving a reason for your stay or showing you have sufficient finances. They will issue a 90-day entry stamp, which is renewable for longer stays."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay in Kosovo for longer than 90 days, you will need to register with the ",["Ministry of Internal Affairs","https://mpb.rks-gov.net/f/45/Temporary-residence-permit-for-foreigners"]," for a residence permit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Kosovo guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/121/kosovo#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Kosovo","https://dogana.rks-gov.net/Individs/Index?individId=1084"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Kosovo","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Kosovo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Kosovo cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, and at large public gatherings and cultural events. Terrorists may target religious sites, including churches."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation in Kosovo is generally stable, but there is a risk of protests."]},{"k":"p","s":["These are usually peaceful, but can lead to some disruption, including to traffic and public transport. Keep up to date with local developments and avoid any large crowds or demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpockets operate in airports and on public transport. Criminals target people they think may be carrying large amounts of cash. Take precautions to protect yourself from street crime by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["only travelling in pre-booked taxis"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing expensive-looking jewellery or watches"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoiding isolated areas especially at night or when walking alone"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Use ATMs inside banks if possible, and check ATMs on the street for signs of tampering. Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read more about ",["how to avoid bank card fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Organised crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Isolated incidents of armed violence and vehicle explosions in major cities are usually linked to organised crime and do not target visitors. However there could be violent incidents in areas visited by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may target 4-wheel-drive and luxury vehicles – they may rob the passengers or try to take the vehicle. Get advice from your accommodation or car hire company about more secure routes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Unexploded landmines and bombs"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk you could encounter landmines or other unexploded weapons when travelling in some remoter parts of Kosovo. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry your passport with you for identification and keep a copy separately in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Kosovo have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taking photographs of military or police installations, personnel or vehicles may lead to difficulties with the authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no laws against same-sex relations in Kosovo. However, Kosovo is still a conservative society and the LGBT+ scene is more tolerated than accepted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Kosovo, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and read the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Kosovo guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/kosovo/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Kosovo. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get a ",["1969 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],". You must carry vehicle registration and ownership documents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Insurance requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need a locally valid insurance policy. European green card vehicle insurance is not valid. You should buy local third-party insurance at the border or from the nearest town at the earliest opportunity. Make sure you have enough cash in euros to pay for insurance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road standards vary from fair to poor. Roads are particularly bad in rural areas and after bad weather. There is a risk of landslides and flooding. Avoid travelling at night if possible. The quality of fuel varies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are sometimes delays at the border crossings between Kosovo and North Macedonia, Kosovo and Albania, and Kosovo and Serbia. These are common around festive periods and during the summer months. Ensure you have food and water in case of delays."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Car hire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many Serbian car hire firms will not allow you to drive their vehicles in Kosovo, and vice-versa, due to concerns about the security situation."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been some incidents where Serbian-registered hire cars have been targeted in more isolated areas of Kosovo."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["The condition of taxis and standard of driving vary. Taxis are readily available in Pristina. Registered taxi firms are the safest option and fares are regulated. These usually need to be ordered by phone, although some are introducing local apps. Operators usually speak a reasonable level of English. International ride-hailing apps are not available."]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis that approach you for a fare are often unofficial and can overcharge. Look for established taxi companies instead of a personally owned vehicle converted to a taxi."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are possible in Kosovo, particularly during dry hot periods from April to October. Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. To avoid starting wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when visiting or driving through countryside"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarette ends are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not light fires or barbecues except in designated and marked areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave any rubbish"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a wildfire, call the emergency services on 112. Follow any advice from the police or local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kosovo lies in a seismically active zone, and earth tremors are common. The last significant earthquake, of magnitude 4.5, happened in 2010 around 90km north of Pristina."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding and landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding and poor road conditions can be a problem after wet weather. There is a risk of landslides, particularly in hilly and mountainous regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check local news reports as flooding or landslides may cause road blockages."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Kosovo. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Northern Kosovo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Whilst there have been recurring tensions across northern Kosovo resulting in sporadic unrest, protests and security incidents, this has improved since 2024. However, northern Kosovo remains politically sensitive and conditions can change quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Localised incidents, including protests and disruptions, can occur with little warning, particularly during periods of heightened political tension. Remain vigilant, monitor local media and stay away from demonstrations and large gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"h","s":["Old landmines and unexploded bombs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Residual landmines and other unexploded bombs and weapons remain in Kosovo from the 1999 conflict. Roads and tracks have been cleared."]},{"k":"p","s":["The main areas of risk are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["along the border with Albania"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Dulje Pass area in central Kosovo"]},{"k":"li","s":["the mountainous region between Kosovo, Albania and Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep to the main roads when travelling in these areas. Most of the remaining dangerous areas are in high mountainous regions covered with dense vegetation. If you see something made of metal or anything suspicious, do not touch it, and report it immediately to the ",["police or the nearest Kosovo Force (KFOR) patrol","https://www.kosovopolice.com/en/numbers-of-police-stations/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 94 from a landline or 194 from a mobile and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Kosovo","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/121/kosovo#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Kosovo","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/121/kosovo"]," including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Crimean Congo Haemorrhagic Fever is endemic in Kosovo. Most cases occur in the region around Malisheva (central Kosovo), but during the summer months other rural areas of Kosovo can be affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mosquito-borne diseases are present, including West Nile virus."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Kosovo. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["High levels of air pollution can occur in Kosovo, particularly in Pristina. You can find further information and advice on air quality on the ",["World Health Organization (WHO)","https://www.who.int/airpollution/en/"]," website and check air quality levels on the ",["World Air Quality Index Website","https://aqicn.org/map/europe/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Kosovo"]},{"k":"p","s":["The public health system in Kosovo is poorly funded. Hospitals lack specialist equipment and there is a widespread shortage of medicines and other essentials. Many doctors and nurses lack training in modern techniques and practices."]},{"k":"p","s":["Treatment is also available at private medical clinics, which are of better quality than the public health system and are relatively affordable. A small payment in cash is required for treatment in the public health system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Kosovo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kosovo-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Kosovo"]},{"k":"p","s":["All emergencies: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 192 from a mobile (92 from a landline)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 193 from a mobile (93 from a landline)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 194 from a mobile (94 from a landline)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Kosovo"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=kosovo"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Kosovo"]," in Kosovo"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Kosovo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kosovo-bereavement-guide"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Kosovo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kosovo-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/kosovo/british-embassy-pristina"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kosovo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":16015,"change":"Updated information about large gatherings in Pristina and other urban areas of Kosovo (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/burnham-in-brussels-why-party-politics-still-defines-the-uks-relationship-with-europe-297081":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-20T14:37Z","sha":"73d4f70c915e117e51049525012239f364c96e97f269615e1389dc9c7e9d2472","read":"https://theconversation.com/burnham-in-brussels-why-party-politics-still-defines-the-uks-relationship-with-europe-297081","bytes":179285,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Burnham in Brussels: why party politics still defines the UK’s relationship with Europe","by":[{"n":"Martin Steven","r":"Senior Lecturer, School of Global Affairs, Lancaster University"}],"pub":"2026-11-20T14:26:34Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Andy Burnham has attended his first EU-UK summit in Brussels with major agreements reached on youth mobility, food exports and carbon emissions. Ultimately though, the prime minister will have understood that this was merely the start of new political negotiations. Back home in the UK, he has started a “national conversation” on the future of UK-EU relations that gained momentum rapidly."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Burnham","https://theconversation.com/topics/andy-burnham-16006"]," held talks with European Council president Antonio Costa and president of the European Commission Ursula von der Leyen. Both Burnham and Costa come from sister social democratic parties and both are former mayors – Burnham of Greater Manchester and Costa of Lisbon. This could make for smoother meetings in future than in the months and years after the 2016 Brexit referendum."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the run up to the talks, the prime minister had repeatedly claimed that the Conservatives ",["failed to get a good deal","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/28/tory-brexit-harder-promised-referendum-andy-burnham"]," from the EU. As part of former prime minister Keir Starmer’s “reset” of relations with Europe, then-business secretary, Peter Kyle, and European Commission vice-president Teresa Ribera ",["signed a deal","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/feb/25/british-public-want-deeper-economic-ties-eu-business-secretary-says"]," committing the UK and the EU to closer cooperation on trade."]},{"k":"p","s":["Like Costa and Burnham, Ribera is also from a European social democratic party (the Spanish Socialist Workers Party, or PSOE. Senior figures in Labour have long admired the ",["electoral success","https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/portugals-power-sharing-success-story-has-vital-lessons-labour/"]," of social democrats in both Spain and Portugal."]},{"k":"p","s":["When it comes to claims of the UK having had a bad deal, there is one explanation that is under-discussed. It has its roots in the internal party politics of the centre-right in Europe. Ahead of the 2009 European Parliament elections, the then-Conservative leader David Cameron ",["decided to leave","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2009/mar/16/david-cameron-epp-barroso"]," the European People’s Party (a bloc of centre-right pro-European parties)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cameron went on to set up a new ",["right-of-centre eurosceptic faction","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2009/may/29/david-cameron-european-union-grandees"]," with parties from Poland and the Czech Republic. But he underestimated how hurt highly influential EU figures like German chancellor Angela Merkel were by the move. So when it came to negotiating a better deal with the EU ahead of the 2016 referendum, Merkel and other figures had not forgotten Cameron’s betrayal. As such, they felt disinclined to ",["meet him half way","https://manchesteruniversitypress.co.uk/9781807072797/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Burnham is walking a fine line"]},{"k":"p","s":["Youth mobility, migration, food exports and emissions are all important issues. But the broader discussion is increasingly about the politics around Brexit rather than the rights and wrongs of Brexit itself."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK is not going to rejoin the EU in the near future. Burnham even said when standing in the Makerfield byelection that first and foremost he wants to ",["sort the consequences of Brexit","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/may/18/andy-burnham-says-he-will-not-try-to-return-uk-to-eu"]," rather than necessarily the outcome."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now Burnham is increasingly focused on the claim that Brexit hasn’t worked for British voters – without saying it was completely wrong. He may understand that aiming to reverse Brexit in a binary way could simply open up new problems. It could even finish his premiership in the same way that it ended the tenures of multiple prime ministers before him."]},{"k":"p","s":["In contrast, however, Burnham understands that he has the political capital to discuss the downsides of Brexit. For now, at least, he can do this in a way that is unlikely to result in much political damage to his government. While not completely without risk, he has calculated that the benefits of discussing Brexit outweigh any costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["These costs could include the fragile “red wall” of Labour seats in northern England and the Midlands. The party knows all too well that this could flip to Reform UK the next time the country goes to the polls."]},{"k":"p","s":["But those voters who have already moved to Reform are something of a sunk cost for Labour. For now, it seems Burnham sees more advantages in drawing voters away from the Liberal Democrats and the Greens than he sees disadvantages in alienating supporters of Reform. Conservative leader Kemi Badenoch appears to be sensitive to the fact that many people disapprove of how the Tories handled Brexit – whether they voted Remain or Leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the height of the Brexit chaos, however, Burnham was mayor of Greater Manchester and so can revisit the issue in a fresh way, untainted by the Westminister turbulence of that time."]},{"k":"p","s":["His predecessor Starmer was frequently seen as being paralysed by caution. Burnham appears to know how to talk about difficult issues lightly and fluently – his own parliamentary seat ",["overwhelmingly voted Leave","https://www.facebook.com/BurnhamGM/posts/in-makerfield-my-constituency-two-thirds-of-people-voted-to-leave-the-eui-unders/1764960541664595/"]," in 2016."]},{"k":"p","s":["He may or may not truly want to see the UK rejoin the EU at some point – he has sometimes sent out ",["mixed signals","https://www.politico.eu/article/andy-burnham-eu-uk-brexit-reset/"]," on the issue. But he certainly has the firm aim of removing the toxicity from the issue and having a ",["“national conversation”","https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news/andy-burnham-brexit-eu-conversation-b3088022.html"],". To do this, the prime minister will have to consider how Westminster relates to Brussels as well as how it relates to constituencies like his own in Makerfield."]}],"chars":4788},"https://theconversation.com/salam-tiga-jari-dan-bendera-one-piece-bagaimana-simbol-budaya-pop-digunakan-untuk-gerakan-sosial-296312":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T02:35Z","sha":"465a1b76df2a92be348164456d3673fc4b315c4be773119b62d9abb77a8b517b","read":"https://theconversation.com/salam-tiga-jari-dan-bendera-one-piece-bagaimana-simbol-budaya-pop-digunakan-untuk-gerakan-sosial-296312","bytes":185851,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘Salam Tiga Jari’ dan bendera ‘One Piece’: Bagaimana simbol budaya pop digunakan untuk gerakan sosial","by":[{"n":"Imam Hanafi","r":"Dosen Linguistik, Universitas Negeri Surabaya"},{"n":"Pratiwi Retnaningdyah","r":"Guru Besar Kajian Sastra dan Budaya, Universitas Negeri Surabaya"}],"pub":"2026-11-27T02:08:43Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Demonstran memakai Salam tiga jari The Hunger Games dan bendera One Piece karena membawa nilai solidaritas dan perlawanan."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Simbol budaya pop mudah digunakan, cepat dipahami, dan ampuh membangun identitas bersama."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Kemunculannya mencerminkan keresahan masyarakat terhadap pungutan, kebakaran hutan, dan mahalnya biaya hidup."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 20 Oktober 2026, mahasiswa dan elemen masyarakat sipil ",["berunjuk rasa di kawasan Tugu Tani, Jakarta Pusat","https://katadata.co.id/berita/nasional/6ad742f4d1b42/mahasiswa-angkat-tiga-jari-di-tugu-tani-evaluasi-dua-tahun-prabowo-gibran"],", untuk mengevaluasi dua tahun pemerintahan Prabowo Subianto-Gibran Rakabuming Raka. Dalam aksi #IndonesiaSadar, para demonstran mengangkat tiga jari sambil menyuarakan tiga seruan: ",["sadar dipalak, sadar dibakar, dan sadar dimiskinkan","https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/jangan-represi-dengarkan-aspirasi-indonesiasadar/10/2026/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gestur serupa kembali muncul ",["pada 28 Oktober 2026","https://www.nu.or.id/nasional/massa-aksi-indonesia-sadar-kompak-acungkan-tiga-jari-sadar-dipalak-sadar-dibakar-sadar-dimiskinkan-dOYur"],", bertepatan dengan Hari Sumpah Pemuda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Salam tiga jari itu diadopsi dari three-finger salute dalam novel dan film ",["_The Hunger Games","https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1392170/"]," _, yang menjadi simbol solidaritas dan perlawanan terhadap penguasa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fenomena ini bukan yang pertama. Menjelang peringatan kemerdekaan Indonesia ke-80 pada 2025, ",["bendera bajak laut","https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/c62766edyx9o"]," dari manga dan anime One Piece juga mewarnai aksi demonstrasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mengapa simbol dari budaya populer begitu mudah digunakan untuk menyuarakan perlawanan?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Bagaimana budaya populer seperti komik bisa memantik perlawanan terhadap rezim","https://theconversation.com/bagaimana-budaya-populer-seperti-komik-bisa-memantik-perlawanan-terhadap-rezim-263629"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Dari makna ke mitos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam ",["semiotika","https://binus.ac.id/malang/2020/01/semiotika/?utm_source=google.com&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=google.com&utm_referrer=google.com"],", ilmu yang mempelajari bagaimana tanda membentuk makna, salam tiga jari memiliki penanda berupa gerakan tangan dengan tiga jari terangkat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam cerita The Hunger Games, gestur ini bermakna ",["penghormatan, kekaguman, dan perpisahan","https://www.degruyterbrill.com/de/document/doi/10.1515/lingvan-2023-0006/html?utm"]," bagi warga Distrik 12. Sementara itu, bendera Jolly Roger milik Bajak Laut Topi Jerami menampilkan tengkorak bertopi jerami dengan dua tulang bersilang. Simbol ini awalnya menandai identitas kelompok bajak laut yang dipimpin Monkey D. Luffy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, tanda dapat ",["bermakna lebih luas","https://scielo.org.za/scielo.php?pid=S1015-87582021000400007&script=sci_arttext&utm"],". Dalam The Hunger Games, misalnya, Katniss Everdeen (tokoh utamanya) mengangkat tiga jari setelah Rue, peserta dari Distrik 11, tewas. Gestur itu menjadi salam perpisahan sekaligus pesan kepada Capitol, penguasa yang mengeksploitasi manusia lewat permainan maut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bendera One Piece juga membawa nilai yang lebih luas dari sekadar identitas bajak laut. ",["Luffy dan krunya","https://amp.dw.com/en/what-the-one-piece-pirate-flag-symbolizes-for-gen-z-protestors/a-74250198?"]," dikenal menjunjung kebebasan, pilihan individu, dan keberanian mengikuti keyakinan sendiri. Mereka juga kerap membela kelompok tertindas dan melawan penguasa yang korup."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nilai-nilai tersebut membuat bendera Topi Jerami kemudian diasosiasikan dengan kebebasan, solidaritas, dan perlawanan terhadap kekuasaan yang menindas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Makna baru mengikuti konteks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika simbol budaya populer digunakan dalam aksi nyata, maknanya ikut menyesuaikan dengan kondisi sosial-politik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Salam tiga jari The Hunger Games pernah digunakan dalam gerakan protes di Thailand dan Myanmar. Di kedua negara, gestur tersebut menjadi ",["simbol perlawanan dan identitas kolektif demonstran","https://anthropological-notebooks.zrc-sazu.si/Notebooks/article/view/94"]," dalam menyikapi ",["persoalan politik yang berbeda","https://www.degruyterbrill.com/document/doi/10.1515/lingvan-2023-0006/html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam gerakan #IndonesiaSadar, salam tiga jari digunakan untuk ",["menyuarakan","https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/jangan-represi-dengarkan-aspirasi-indonesiasadar/10/2026/"]," keresahan atas pungutan, kebakaran hutan, dan pemiskinan. Nilai solidaritas dan perlawanan tetap sama, tetapi persoalan yang disuarakan berubah mengikuti konteks lokal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bendera One Piece memiliki perjalanan yang sedikit berbeda. Jika salam tiga jari mengalami perluasan makna sejak dalam cerita, bendera Topi Jerami lebih banyak membawa nilai yang memang sudah melekat pada karakter dan kisahnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, bendera tersebut mulai dikibarkan menjelang peringatan kemerdekaan ke-80 sebagai ekspresi ketidakpuasan terhadap pemerintah. Penggunaannya berkaitan dengan ",["kritik terhadap kebijakan","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c3ezvj4d111o"]," yang dianggap tidak mencerminkan aspirasi masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Pelarangan bendera One Piece: Negara makin paranoid, demokrasi makin sempit","https://theconversation.com/pelarangan-bendera-one-piece-negara-makin-paranoid-demokrasi-makin-sempit-262517"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Fenomena serupa juga muncul di Filipina dan Nepal. ",["Di Filipina","https://www.cnbcindonesia.com/news/20250921181540-7-668882/potret-chaos-demo-filipina-massa-vs-polisi-bendera-one-piece-berkibar"],", bendera One Piece terlihat dalam demonstrasi yang menyoroti dugaan korupsi dana penanggulangan banjir. ",["Di Nepal","https://www.tempo.co/internasional/setelah-indonesia-bendera-one-piece-berkibar-dalam-protes-di-nepal-2068473"],", simbol tersebut juga muncul dalam aksi protes terhadap kebijakan pemerintah dan korupsi."]},{"k":"h","s":["Media sosial bisa menguatkan atau malah mengubah makna"]},{"k":"p","s":["Media sosial membuat simbol budaya pop semakin mudah menyebar dan membentuk makna baru. Dalam aksi protes, platform seperti X, Instagram, dan YouTube bukan ",["hanya alat komunikasi","https://www.eco-business.com/id/opinion/hashtags-hurt-hashtags-heal-too/"],", tetapi juga ruang untuk membangun solidaritas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ada beberapa alasan simbol budaya pop cocok digunakan dalam gerakan sosial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertama, simbolnya mudah dibuat ulang. Salam tiga jari tidak membutuhkan biaya, sedangkan bendera One Piece bisa dicetak, dijahit, atau digambar. Pada Agustus 2025, warganet bahkan mengganti ",["foto profil","https://binus.ac.id/character-building/2025/09/kisah-dalam-sejarah-tren-brave-pink-hero-green/"]," dengan filter warna merah muda dan hijau melalui situs pembuat gambar sederhana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua, simbol ini ",["mudah dipahami","https://spkb.blot.im/_readings/EncodingDecoding_HALL_1980.pdf"]," oleh orang yang mengenal kisahnya. Penggemar The Hunger Games atau One Piece dapat menangkap pesan solidaritas dan perlawanan tanpa perlu penjelasan panjang. Satu foto atau unggahan bisa menyampaikan pesan yang cukup kuat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketiga, simbol budaya pop tumbuh dalam ",["budaya partisipatif","https://books.google.co.id/books/about/Participatory_Culture_in_a_Networked_Era.html?hl=id&id=C_6aoAEACAAJ&redir_esc=y"],": pengguna bukan hanya mengonsumsi konten, tetapi juga membagikan, mengubah, dan memberi makna baru. Ketika simbol yang sama terus digunakan, ia menjadi penanda identitas dan rasa memiliki, bahkan bagi orang yang tidak berada di lokasi demonstrasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tagar bekerja dengan cara serupa. Penggunaan #IndonesiaSadar atau gambar tiga jari bukan sekadar ",["menyebarkan informasi","https://www.degruyterbrill.com/document/doi/10.18574/nyu/9780814743515.001.0001/html"],", tetapi juga dapat menunjukkan keberpihakan seseorang terhadap gerakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, ketika beredar luas di media sosial, simbol juga bisa berubah menjadi meme, ",["dipotong, diubah, atau ditafsirkan ulang","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/14703572241283871?"],". Maknanya ",["tidak selalu lagi","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/1369118X.2015.1043319"]," berada di tangan pembuat atau pengguna awal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ketika gestur menjadi pernyataan sosial"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi generasi yang tumbuh bersama novel, film, manga, dan anime, simbol-simbol tersebut menjadi bahasa bersama untuk menyampaikan keresahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Apalagi ketika saluran aspirasi resmi terasa tidak cukup, simbol yang akrab dan mudah dikenali dapat menjadi cara untuk berbicara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ketika Wibu turun aksi: kesadaran politik kritis kaum muda kembali bangkit","https://theconversation.com/ketika-wibu-turun-aksi-kesadaran-politik-kritis-kaum-muda-kembali-bangkit-238565"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, simbol perlawanan bisa dipinjam pihak lain, termasuk politikus yang ingin tampak dekat dengan anak muda. Wakil Presiden ",["Gibran Rakabuming Raka","https://www.hukumonline.com/berita/a/pengibaran-bendera-one-piece--bentuk-ekspresi-bukan-makar-lt6890804747ad9?page=all"],", misalnya, pernah memakai simbol One Piece. Bahkan belakangan ini, baik salam tiga jari maupun bendera Topi Jerami disebut-sebut sebagai ",["barang bukti dugaan makar.","https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/cmkgk62erpneo"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Jadi, kekuatan simbol tidak hanya ditentukan oleh bentuknya, tetapi juga oleh siapa yang menggunakannya, dalam konteks apa, dan pesan apa yang ingin disampaikan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tiga jari yang teracung dan bendera bajak laut yang berkibar sebaiknya dibaca sebagai pesan, bukan ancaman. Sebab, di balik gestur fiksi itu, ada keluhan yang nyata: pungutan, asap kebakaran hutan, dan ",["biaya hidup yang terus naik","https://asianews.network/thousands-of-protesters-rally-in-jakarta-against-haze-rising-living-costs/"]," —tinggal pemerintah mau mendengarnya atau tidak."]}],"chars":6677},"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-victorias-message-to-federal-labor-voters-can-turn-on-a-dime-297275":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-28T13:18Z","sha":"79c30898cc45041f46159c99b16e3218f7e52102f12b27fe21660891e85c0977","read":"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-victorias-message-to-federal-labor-voters-can-turn-on-a-dime-297275","bytes":182179,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"View from The Hill: Victoria’s message to federal Labor – voters can turn on a dime","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-28T12:27:00Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Victorians have delivered a savage indictment of a government they grew to hate, only four years after giving it an increased majority."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is a blunt message – including to the Albanese government – about how quickly opinion can change and, when it does, how harsh voters’ judgement can be."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jess Wilson, 36 years old and with only one parliamentary term under her belt, becomes Victoria’s new premier. The fact voters have given her a massive majority will make the huge task ahead of her at least somewhat easier."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor’s vote has plunged from about 37% last election to under 20% late on Saturday night. Far from helping revive Labor, Ben Carroll, installed at five minutes to midnight, lost his own seat. The seat vacated by former premier Jacinta Allan has also gone among the swathe of others."]},{"k":"p","s":["One Nation has had strong support – about one in five of the primary votes – but preferences mean it’s unclear what this means for seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pauline Hanson told her party faithful: “One Nation is snapping at the heels of the political establishment. [ …] One Nation won’t be slowing down.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greens have increased their numbers from four lower house seats in the last parliament, as many progressive voters, protesting against Labor, moved to them."]},{"k":"p","s":["It wasn’t clear on Saturday night whether Labor or the Greens would be the official opposition."]},{"k":"p","s":["The result was largely centred on state factors – including crime, financial mismanagement, corruption particularly driven by the CFMEU, potholes, and political arrogance."]},{"k":"p","s":["And, of course, cost of living – which is a crossover issue with federal politics. Also feeding into the picture were the broader national climate of economic malaise (rising inflation, interest rates, unemployment), an unpopular federal government and a fragmenting party system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite being mainly about state issues, the Victorian outcome will be closely scrutinised for its likely federal fallout and how this will affect the psychology of Labor, the Coalition, One Nation and the Greens nationally."]},{"k":"p","s":["Deputy Prime Minister Richard Marles spoke to Anthony Albanese during the evening about the devastating picture."]},{"k":"p","s":["“A bad night for Labor and we both shared that sentiment when we spoke to each other about it,” he told the ABC. “In terms of our concern and what we do, we are focused in terms of administering the federal government in the best way we can to support working Australians.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Marles admitted that, “it is obviously the case that a backdrop to this is a pretty challenging economy right now. We’ve had two interest rate rises in recent times and that forms the backdrop of what’s occurred here.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rout tells the Albanese government that however well protected a party may feel by having a big majority, even the largest buffer is no guarantee when a volatile electorate has become hyper-angry."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the Liberals, the state result is a hefty shot of adrenaline. It comes when a few encouraging signs have been appearing for the federal Coalition and Angus Taylor."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Melbourne at the Liberal celebration on Saturday night, Taylor declared, “The Liberal Party is back in town”. Taylor, incidentally, could take a few lessons from Wilson in the art of campaigning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Deputy Liberal leader Jane Hume was quick to claim federal factors played into the result, pointing to small businesses collapsing."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the adrenaline doesn’t last indefinitely. Both the Liberals and the Nationals have to brace themselves for a bad result in New South Wales at the March state election."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Albanese government may hope the defeat in Victoria could mean now voters have taken out their vengeance against state Labor, the slate may be cleaner by the time of the federal election. Labor super-optimists might hope the new state government will have stuffed up, to a greater or lesser extent, by 2028."]},{"k":"p","s":["But if Wilson performs well that could potentially help the prospects for federal Liberals. Importantly, there will be a great deal more Coalition electoral infrastructure with all those new members, and that should assist the Coalition federally in a state where it has been almost wiped out federally and must recapture ground to have any chance of national office."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wilson has run a sustained and strong campaign as opposition leader; impressively, she has brought and kept together what had been a dysfunctional Liberal Party."]},{"k":"p","s":["But governing brings different challenges, requiring its own skill set. Not only has Wilson never been a minister – she is taking over a state fractured on various fronts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Identifying problems is one thing, fixing them is something else entirely."]},{"k":"p","s":["And then she has to maintain discipline in her own ranks, making sure her government is not undermined by hubris, or the sheer bloody-mindedness for which the Victorian Liberals have been notorious."]},{"k":"p","s":["She has travelled an amazing journey to this point. Now she starts the mountain climb."]}],"chars":4850}};
